GCF columnar format (internal/gcf):
The GCF "generic profile" text format implemented in internal/gcf originates
from gcf-typescript, Copyright (c) Blackwell Systems
(https://github.com/blackwell-systems/gcf-typescript), licensed under the MIT
License, as vendored into OmniRoute
(https://github.com/diegosouzapw/OmniRoute), also MIT-licensed. internal/gcf
is an independent Go reimplementation of the format (scalars-only subset);
no upstream source code was copied.

Compose templates adapted from hyperframes-student-kit (render/compose-templates):
stat-card, section-title, callout-label and checklist-card are adapted from card
designs in hyperframes-student-kit, pinned at commit 0d30152, which is licensed
under the MIT License with an additional use permission for its style library
and templates. Each template is a rewrite in CSS keyframes of the card's layout
and motion; no upstream source file was copied. The kit's licence texts are kept
verbatim in render/compose-templates/_third_party/hyperframes-student-kit/, whose
PROVENANCE.md records the source repository, the pinned commit, and what was
taken and what was not.

ComfyUI workflow template fixtures (render/testdata/templates-catalog/):
The workflow files there are trimmed excerpts of templates from Comfy-Org/workflow_templates
(https://github.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates), Copyright (c) 2023-present Comfy Org,
licensed under the MIT License. The licence text is kept beside them in
LICENSE-comfy-workflow-templates.txt. They are test inputs only and are not shipped.

Search-results compaction rung (internal/agent/rung_search.go):
The idea of thinning search results by relevance to the task (BM25 ranking, a cap per
file, diversity across files, a boost for error lines) is documented by the Headroom
project, Copyright 2025 Headroom Contributors (https://github.com/headroomlabs-ai/headroom),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The caps used here (30 lines in total, 5 per
file, 15 files) are the defaults of the SearchCompressor configuration listed on its
documentation page docs/content/docs/text-and-logs.mdx
(https://github.com/headroomlabs-ai/headroom/blob/main/docs/content/docs/text-and-logs.mdx).
internal/agent/rung_search.go is an independent, clean-room Go implementation written from
that documented behaviour; no upstream source code was read or copied. The rung is off by default.
